WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.140
Company pensions, from the Rampersad Branch.
How they work — and how we run one, end to
end.

2
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.614
Your best people are hard to replace. A raise
is spent by Friday.

3
00:00:11.614 --> 00:00:13.420
A pension is a reason to stay.

4
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.256
The company pays the premium. Guardian holds
the policy.

5
00:00:21.256 --> 00:00:24.640
And the value builds for your employee — and
for their family.

6
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:31.968
Under Section 134, the company owns the
policy, and deducts every dollar it pays.

7
00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.700
The employee is the person it pays out to.

8
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.181
There is a ceiling.

9
00:00:37.181 --> 00:00:41.880
And because the contribution itself counts as
income, it has to be solved — not multiplied.

10
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:50.633
Two tests decide it. One third of chargeable
income, or twenty per cent of emolument
income.

11
00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:54.180
And here's the rule — you take the greater.
Never both.

12
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.278
So, on a salary of two hundred and forty
thousand —

13
00:00:58.278 --> 00:01:02.929
the most the company can put in is sixty-two
thousand, six hundred and sixty dollars a
year.

14
00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.900
And every dollar of that is deductible.

15
00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.800
The company signs the B.I.R.

16
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.200
request and Declaration Two, and sends
certified company documents with them.

17
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.872
The site opens by asking who is signing in.

18
00:01:17.872 --> 00:01:21.600
Agent, employer, or employee — each one gets
their own view.

19
00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:29.440
Agents type a case once. It computes live,
shows its working, and prints the B.I.R. form.

20
00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.690
The real Guardian forms fill themselves as you
type.

21
00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:38.220
Both declarations, and the salary deduction.

22
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:46.900
Then one PDF. Every form, in submission order
— fifteen pages on a typical case.

23
00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:53.340
And the employee receives their own copy,
written in plain language.

24
00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.640
Enrolling is two-sided. The employer completes
one form.

25
00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.580
And the moment they submit — we write to their
employee.

26
00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.831
The employee finishes their part in about ten
minutes, on their phone.

27
00:02:09.831 --> 00:02:12.900
We remind them at nine each morning, until it
is in.

28
00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.015
From there, nobody has to chase anyone.

29
00:02:17.015 --> 00:02:20.220
Both sides watch five steps — all the way to
delivery.

30
00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.740
Employers sign in with one code, and see their
whole schedule.

31
00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.320
Employees see one line. Their own — and nobody
else's.

32
00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:44.478
Nothing is returned without a matching code.
Every lookup is logged.

33
00:02:44.478 --> 00:02:46.700
And only the branch can change a record.

34
00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:54.820
Pension plan T T dot com. Open it, answer who
you are — and the rest is already built.
